A||||10||bHooper||Regarding Chain Letters... YOU KNOW WHO YOU ARE!||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||03-21-2001||11:03 PM||||i, as well as several other people in the CAROLINA are, received a chain letter on my personel email.  i do not apreciate this.  therefore i have taken the time to post the following information about chain letters!<P>hoop<P><I>Chain letters represent another kind of pyramid scheme. According to the U.S. Postal Inspection Service definition, a chain letter is "a get-rich-quick scheme that promises that your mail box will soon be stuffed full of cash if you decide to participate. You're told you can make thousands of dollars every<BR> month if you follow the detailed instructions in the letter. <P>"There's at least one problem with chain letters," the agency noted. "They're illegal if they request money or other items of value and promise a substantial return to the participants." Importantly, anyone participating can be subject to prosecution. <P>"Recently, high-tech chain letters have begun surfacing. They may be disseminated over the Internet or require the copying and mailing of computer disks rather than paper. Regardless of what technology is used to advance the scheme, if the mail is used at any step along the way, it is still illegal,"<BR> the Inspection Service said. <P>And, besides being illegal, the numbers don't really add up. "The main thing to remember is that a chain letter is simply a bad investment," according to the USPIS. "You certainly won't get rich. You will receive little or no money."</I><BR>||||reg||1
